        "title": "Nonlinear and Convex Optimization - Convexity, KKT, Interior-Point",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Once the objective or constraints become nonlinear, the clean vertex story of LP (file 01) is gone — but a deeper structure replaces it: **convexity**. For convex problems, local optimality implies global optimality, the **KKT conditions** certify optima (generalizing LP's complementary slackness), and **interior-point methods** solve them in polynomial time. Nonconvex problems lose all of this and you settle for stationary points."
    }
